  "instruction": "Open /home/user/Desktop/two_sided_part.step in FreeCAD 0.21.2 Path/CAM. The source is a centered 120 x 80 x 18 mm plate. Create two independent native FreeCAD Path Jobs: Side A uses G54 and a T1 D8 flat end mill to cut a centered 60 x 36 mm through pocket from Z18 to Z0; Side B uses G55 and a flipped-side coordinate system, T2 D6 drill for four through pilot holes at (-45,-25), (45,-25), (-45,25), (45,25), and T3 D8 flat end mill as the counterbore cutter for four D12 counterbores, 4 mm deep from the B side. Use S7000 rpm and F500 mm/min for all tools. Generate the native linuxcnc-posted files exactly /home/user/Desktop/task-17_A.nc and /home/user/Desktop/task-17_B.nc, and save the editable native document as /home/user/Desktop/task-17_real.fcstd. Both jobs must be recomputable and their native operations must be Up-to-date.",
